00:38:47,695 --> 00:38:48,857
Charge them with what?

505
00:38:49,029 --> 00:38:51,900
In a Rico case, if you can charge one of them with a felony...

506
00:38:52,074 --> 00:38:54,647
You can charge all of them with it. that's great.

507
00:38:56,036 --> 00:38:57,945
Mr. Lau.

508
00:38:58,956 --> 00:39:02,954
What kind of details do you have about this communal fund?

509
00:39:03,127 --> 00:39:04,751
- ledgers...? - immunity, protection...

510
00:39:04,920 --> 00:39:08,372
...a chartered plane back to hong kong. - after you testify in open court.

511
00:39:08,549 --> 00:39:10,874
I'm just curious. with all your clients locked up...

512
00:39:11,218 --> 00:39:13,425
...what's gonna happen with all that money?

513
00:39:13,596 --> 00:39:16,715
Like I said, I'm good with calculation.

514
00:39:16,890 --> 00:39:21,552
He can't go to county. I'll keep him here in the holding cells.

515
00:39:21,729 --> 00:39:24,267
What is this, Gordon, your fortress?

516
00:39:24,565 --> 00:39:27,234
Well, you trust them over at county?

517
00:39:27,401 --> 00:39:29,228
I don't trust them here.

518
00:39:30,988 --> 00:39:32,482
Lau stays.

519
00:39:32,948 --> 00:39:35,522
Well, I don't know about mr. Lau's travel arrangements...

520
00:39:35,701 --> 00:39:37,492
... but I'm sure glad he's back.

521
00:39:37,661 --> 00:39:40,117
Put word out. we hire the clown.

522
00:39:42,917 --> 00:39:46,748
He was right. we have to fix real problem.

523
00:39:47,254 --> 00:39:48,369
Batman.

524
00:39:52,927 --> 00:39:56,841
- I'm not aware of any participation... - our boy looks good on the tube.

525
00:39:57,348 --> 00:40:00,099
You sure you wanna embarrass me in front of my friends?

526
00:40:00,267 --> 00:40:03,932
Oh, don't worry. they're coming too.

527
00:40:10,778 --> 00:40:12,605
Have a nice trip. see you next fall.

528
00:40:12,780 --> 00:40:14,607
Seven hundred twelve counts of extortion.

529
00:40:14,782 --> 00:40:17,189
Eight hundred and forty-nine counts of racketeering.

530
00:40:17,368 --> 00:40:19,906
Two hundred and forty-six counts of fraud.

531
00:40:20,079 --> 00:40:22,914
Eighty-seven counts of conspiracy murder.

532
00:40:23,832 --> 00:40:26,952
Five hundred and twenty-seven counts of obstruction of justice.

533
00:40:27,378 --> 00:40:28,753
How do the defendants plead?

534
00:40:35,928 --> 00:40:36,959
Order in the court.

535
00:40:37,137 --> 00:40:39,628
Five hundred and forty-nine criminals at once.

536
00:40:39,807 --> 00:40:42,298
How did you convince Surrillo to hear this farce?

537
00:40:42,476 --> 00:40:46,604
She shares my enthusiasm for justice. after all, she is a judge.

538
00:40:46,772 --> 00:40:49,808
Even if you blow enough smoke to get convictions out of Surrillo...

539
00:40:49,984 --> 00:40:52,557
...you're gonna set a new record at appeals.

540
00:40:52,736 --> 00:40:55,227
It won't matter. the head guys make bail, sure.

541
00:40:55,406 --> 00:40:57,813
But the midlevel guys, they can't.

542
00:40:57,992 --> 00:40:59,818
They can't afford to be off the streets.

543
00:40:59,994 --> 00:41:02,117
They'll cut deals that include some jail time.

544
00:41:02,288 --> 00:41:05,288
Think of all you could do with 18 months of clean streets.

545
00:41:06,834 --> 00:41:09,954
Mr. mayor, you can't... - no, get out. both of you.

546
00:41:14,133 --> 00:41:15,675
Sit down.

547
00:41:20,639 --> 00:41:23,640
The public likes you. that's the only reason that this might fly.

548
00:41:23,809 --> 00:41:25,137
But that means it's on you.

549
00:41:25,311 --> 00:41:28,347
They're all gonna come after you now, and not just the mob.

550
00:41:28,522 --> 00:41:32,354
Politicians, journalists, cops.

551
00:41:32,526 --> 00:41:35,017
Anyone whose wallet's about to get lighter.

552
00:41:35,195 --> 00:41:37,865
Are you up to it? you'd better be.

553
00:41:38,032 --> 00:41:40,155
Because they get anything on you...

554
00:41:40,326 --> 00:41:42,631
...and those criminals are back on the streets,

555
00:41:42,632 --> 00:41:45,118
followed swiftly by you and me

556
00:41:45,289 --> 00:41:46,569
Jesus!

557
00:42:07,728 --> 00:42:10,184
I think your fundraiser will be a great success, sir.

558
00:42:10,356 --> 00:42:13,025
And why do you think I wanna hold a party for Harvey Dent?

559
00:42:13,046 --> 00:42:16,276
I assumed it was your usual reason for socializing beyond myself...

560
00:42:16,278 --> 00:42:18,520
...and the scum of Gotham's underbelly:

561
00:42:18,656 --> 00:42:20,447
To try to impress miss Dawes.

562
00:42:20,616 --> 00:42:24,696
Very droll, but very wrong. actually, it's Dent.

563
00:42:24,870 --> 00:42:27,741
Police released video footage found concealed on the body.

564
00:42:27,915 --> 00:42:30,536
Sensitive viewers, be aware. the image is disturbing.

565
00:42:30,709 --> 00:42:32,916
Tell them your name.

566
00:42:33,087 --> 00:42:34,747
Brian Douglas.

567
00:42:36,340 --> 00:42:38,665
And are you the real batman?

568
00:42:38,842 --> 00:42:39,874
No. no?

569
00:42:40,052 --> 00:42:42,009
- no. - no?

570
00:42:42,179 --> 00:42:43,887
Then why do you dress up like him?

571
00:42:46,642 --> 00:42:50,722
Because he's a symbol that we don't have to be afraid of scum like you.

572
00:42:50,896 --> 00:42:54,230
Yeah. you do, Brian. you really do.

573
00:42:54,400 --> 00:42:58,018
Huh? yeah. oh, shh, shh, shh.

574
00:42:58,195 --> 00:43:02,656
So you think batman's made Gotham a better place? hm?

575
00:43:02,866 --> 00:43:04,409
Look at me.

576
00:43:04,577 --> 00:43:06,865
Look at me!

577
00:43:10,624 --> 00:43:14,124
You see, this is how crazy batman's made Gotham.

578
00:43:14,295 --> 00:43:16,583
You want order in Gotham...

579
00:43:16,922 --> 00:43:21,335
... batman must take off his mask and turn himself in.

580
00:43:21,510 --> 00:43:25,294
Oh, and every day he doesn't, people will die.

581
00:43:25,639 --> 00:43:27,762
Starting tonight.

582
00:43:28,183 --> 00:43:30,390
I'm a man of my word.

583
00:43:47,661 --> 00:43:50,496
Harvey Dent, scourge of the underworld...

584
00:43:50,664 --> 00:43:53,749
...scared stiff by the trust-fund brigade.

585
00:43:53,918 --> 00:43:55,163
- I'll be back. - Rachel.

586
00:43:55,336 --> 00:43:58,171
A little liquid courage, mr. Dent?

587
00:43:58,339 --> 00:44:00,746
- thank you. Alfred, right? - that's right, sir.

588
00:44:00,925 --> 00:44:04,210
Rachel talks about you all the time. you've known her her whole life.

589
00:44:04,386 --> 00:44:05,631
Not yet, sir.

590
00:44:07,932 --> 00:44:10,173
Any psychotic ex-boyfriends I should be aware of?

591
00:44:10,351 --> 00:44:12,592
Oh, you have no idea.

592
00:44:31,538 --> 00:44:32,949
I'm sorry that I'm late.

593
00:44:33,123 --> 00:44:35,496
I'm glad to see that you all got started without me.

594
00:44:35,668 --> 00:44:39,368
Now, where is Harvey? where...?

595
00:44:39,546 --> 00:44:41,954
Harvey Dent, the man of the hour.

596
00:44:42,132 --> 00:44:43,461
Where's Rachel Dawes?

597
00:44:43,634 --> 00:44:46,006
She is my oldest friend. come here.

598
00:44:46,178 --> 00:44:48,669
When Rachel first told me she was dating Harvey Dent...

599
00:44:48,847 --> 00:44:50,046
...I had one thing to say

600
00:44:50,266 --> 00:44:52,673
"the guy from those god-awful campaign commercials?"

601
00:44:52,851 --> 00:44:56,683
"i believe in Harvey Dent." yeah, nice slogan, Harvey.

602
00:44:56,855 --> 00:44:58,848
But it caught Rachel's attention.

603
00:44:59,024 --> 00:45:02,025
And then I started to pay attention to Harvey...

604
00:45:02,444 --> 00:45:05,730
...and all that he's been doing as our new da.

605
00:45:05,906 --> 00:45:07,698
And you know what?

606
00:45:09,743 --> 00:45:11,238
I believe in Harvey Dent.

607
00:45:11,412 --> 00:45:14,994
I believe that on his watch, Gotham can feel...

608
00:45:15,165 --> 00:45:18,831
...a little safer, a little more optimistic.

609
00:45:20,254 --> 00:45:24,583
Look at this face. this is the face of Gotham's bright future.

610
00:45:24,758 --> 00:45:26,917
To Harvey Dent. let's hear it for him.

611
00:45:27,303 --> 00:45:28,845
Harvey.

612
00:45:38,355 --> 00:45:39,814
Harvey may not know you well enough...

613
00:45:39,982 --> 00:45:41,939
...to understand you're making fun of him...

614
00:45:42,109 --> 00:45:44,102
...but I do. - no, I meant every word.

615
00:45:45,446 --> 00:45:48,363
You know that day that you once told me about...

616
00:45:48,532 --> 00:45:50,608
...when Gotham would no longer need batman?

617
00:45:50,784 --> 00:45:52,694
- it's coming. - Bruce.

618
00:45:53,537 --> 00:45:56,083
- you can't ask me to wait for that.

619
00:45:56,084 --> 00:45:59,124
- it's happening now. Harvey is that hero

620
00:45:59,293 --> 00:46:01,022
He locked up half of the city's

621
00:46:01,023 --> 00:46:03,754
Criminals, and he did it without wearing a mask

622
00:46:03,923 --> 00:46:06,129
Gotham needs a hero with a face.

623
00:46:06,967 --> 00:46:09,256
You can throw a party, Wayne, I'll give you that.

624
00:46:10,638 --> 00:46:12,547
Thanks again.

625
00:46:13,349 --> 00:46:15,057
You mind if I borrow Rachel?

626
00:46:18,520 --> 00:46:20,893
Lieutenant, that Joker card pinned to the body?

627
00:46:21,065 --> 00:46:22,808
Forensics found three sets of dna.

628
00:46:22,983 --> 00:46:24,394
- any matches? - all three.

629
00:46:24,568 --> 00:46:28,067
The dna belongs to judge Surrillo, Harvey Dent and commissioner loeb.

630
00:46:28,238 --> 00:46:30,231
The Joker's telling us who he's targeting.

631
00:46:30,407 --> 00:46:33,278
Get a unit over to Surrillo's house. tell Wuertz to find Dent.

632
00:46:33,452 --> 00:46:35,492
Protective custody. where's the commissioner?

633
00:46:35,663 --> 00:46:37,157
- city hall. - seal the building.

634
00:46:37,331 --> 00:46:39,324
- no one in or out till I get there. - got it.

635
00:46:51,637 --> 00:46:54,009
Gordon. what are you up to?

636
00:46:54,181 --> 00:46:57,431
We're secure. I want a floor-by-floor search of the entire building.

637
00:46:57,601 --> 00:47:00,175
We believe the Joker's made a threat against your life.

638
00:47:00,354 --> 00:47:01,765
These are dangerous people.

639
00:47:01,939 --> 00:47:03,682
You're not giving me a lot of information.

640
00:47:03,857 --> 00:47:05,815
Even we don't know where you're going.

641
00:47:05,985 --> 00:47:09,318
Take the envelope, get in, open it. it'll tell you where you're headed.

642
00:47:13,158 --> 00:47:15,068
You can't leave me alone with these people.

643
00:47:15,244 --> 00:47:18,280
The whole mob's after you and you're worried about these guys?

644
00:47:18,455 --> 00:47:20,413
Compared to this, the mob doesn't scare me.

645
00:47:20,583 --> 00:47:24,165
Gordon, you're unlikely to discover this for yourself, so...

646
00:47:24,336 --> 00:47:28,416
...take my word, the police commissioner earns a lot of threats.

647
00:47:28,591 --> 00:47:34,130
I found the appropriate response to these situations a long time ago.

648
00:47:34,346 --> 00:47:36,588
Them gunning for you makes you see things clearly.

649
00:47:36,765 --> 00:47:38,094
Yeah, I bet.

650
00:47:38,267 --> 00:47:42,561
Yeah. it makes you think about things you couldn't stand losing...

651
00:47:42,730 --> 00:47:44,722
...about who you wanna spend your life with.

652
00:47:44,898 --> 00:47:47,899
- that's a pretty big commitment. - not if the mob has their way.

653
00:47:53,115 --> 00:47:55,820
You get to explain to my wife...

654
00:47:56,744 --> 00:47:58,321
...why I'm late for dinner.

655
00:47:58,495 --> 00:48:01,662
Sir, the Joker card had traces of your dna on it.

656
00:48:03,250 --> 00:48:05,872
- don't do that. - all right.

657
00:48:06,420 --> 00:48:09,338
- let's be serious, then. - okay.

658
00:48:09,673 --> 00:48:10,705
What's your answer?

659
00:48:16,889 --> 00:48:18,383
I don't have an answer.

660
00:48:20,559 --> 00:48:21,590
How'd they get my dna?

661
00:48:21,769 --> 00:48:23,927
Somebody with access to your office or house...

662
00:48:24,104 --> 00:48:26,726
...must have lifted a tissue or a glass... wait! wait!

663
00:48:26,899 --> 00:48:29,816
- well, I guess no answer is a no. - Harvey.

664
00:48:29,985 --> 00:48:32,108
- it's someone else, isn't it? - Harvey.

665
00:48:32,279 --> 00:48:35,446
Just tell me it's not Wayne. the guy's a complete f...

666
00:48:35,950 --> 00:48:37,408
What are you doing?

667
00:48:48,587 --> 00:48:49,618
Oh, shit.

668
00:48:55,803 --> 00:48:57,546
Get a medic!

669
00:49:00,975 --> 00:49:02,089
They've come for him.

670
00:49:03,602 --> 00:49:04,765
We made it.

671
00:49:07,356 --> 00:49:08,387
Stay hidden.

672
00:49:10,651 --> 00:49:13,984
Good evening, ladies and gentlemen.

673
00:49:16,907 --> 00:49:20,821
We are tonight's entertainment.

674
00:49:21,662 --> 00:49:23,987
I only have one question:

675
00:49:24,206 --> 00:49:27,741
Where is Harvey Dent?

676
00:49:37,219 --> 00:49:39,295
You know where Harvey is? you know who he is?

677
00:49:39,471 --> 00:49:40,752
Hands up, pretty boy.

678
00:49:47,896 --> 00:49:50,684
Do you know where I can find Harvey? I need to talk to him.

679
00:49:50,858 --> 00:49:53,693
Just something little, huh? no.

680
00:49:55,988 --> 00:49:58,740
What's going on out there? Wayne!

681
00:50:00,200 --> 00:50:01,576
Oh, thank god, you've got a panic room.

682
00:50:01,744 --> 00:50:02,906
Hey, wait...

683
00:50:03,495 --> 00:50:05,287
Oh, you gotta be kidding me.

684
00:50:05,581 --> 00:50:07,573
You know, I'll settle for his loved ones.

685
00:50:07,750 --> 00:50:11,249
We're not intimidated by thugs.

686
00:50:12,212 --> 00:50:13,920
You know...

687
00:50:15,549 --> 00:50:18,550
...you remind me of my father.

688
00:50:19,011 --> 00:50:20,838
I hated my father.

689
00:50:21,013 --> 00:50:23,052
Okay, stop.

690
00:50:26,894 --> 00:50:29,729
Well, hello, beautiful.

691
00:50:31,899 --> 00:50:35,731
You must be Harvey's squeeze. hm?

692
00:50:36,111 --> 00:50:38,602
And you are beautiful.

693
00:50:45,537 --> 00:50:49,405
You look nervous. is it the scars?

694
00:50:50,334 --> 00:50:52,540
You wanna know how I got them?

695
00:50:53,754 --> 00:50:56,292
Come here. hey.

696
00:50:56,674 --> 00:50:58,382
Look at me.

697
00:50:58,842 --> 00:51:03,588
So I had a wife. she was beautiful, like you...

698
00:51:03,847 --> 00:51:08,059
...who tells me I worry too much...

699
00:51:08,227 --> 00:51:11,144
...who tells me I ought to smile more...

700
00:51:11,313 --> 00:51:16,818
...who gambles and gets in deep with the sharks. hey.

701
00:51:17,236 --> 00:51:19,643
One day they carve her face.

702
00:51:20,155 --> 00:51:24,402
And we have no money for surgeries. she can't take it.

703
00:51:24,785 --> 00:51:28,284
I just wanna see her smile again. hm?

704
00:51:28,622 --> 00:51:31,540
I just want her to know that I don't care about the scars.

705
00:51:32,084 --> 00:51:33,626
So...

706
00:51:34,211 --> 00:51:37,876
...i stick a razor in my mouth and do this...

707
00:51:38,340 --> 00:51:39,716
...to myself.

708
00:51:40,009 --> 00:51:45,086
And you know what? she can't stand the sight of me.

709
00:51:45,264 --> 00:51:46,806
She leaves.

710
00:51:47,516 --> 00:51:49,924
Now I see the funny side.

711
00:51:50,811 --> 00:51:52,389
Now I'm always smiling.

712
00:51:55,816 --> 00:51:59,150
You got a little fight in you. I like that.

713
00:51:59,320 --> 00:52:00,648
Then you're gonna love me.

714
00:52:28,807 --> 00:52:30,005
Drop the gun.

715
00:52:30,184 --> 00:52:32,805
Oh, sure. you just take off your little mask...

716
00:52:32,978 --> 00:52:35,185
...and show us all who you really are. hm?

717
00:52:40,819 --> 00:52:42,017
Let her go.

718
00:52:42,821 --> 00:52:44,232
Very poor choice of words.

719
00:53:07,054 --> 00:53:08,928
Are you all right?

720
00:53:11,183 --> 00:53:13,555
Let's not do that again.

721
00:53:13,852 --> 00:53:16,343
- is Harvey okay? - he's safe.

722
00:53:17,898 --> 00:53:19,227
Thank you.

723
00:53:19,566 --> 00:53:20,598
Jim, it's over.

724
00:53:20,776 --> 00:53:23,349
As long as they don't get to Lau, we've cut off their funds.

725
00:53:23,529 --> 00:53:25,023
The prosecution's over.

726
00:53:25,197 --> 00:53:26,857
Nobody's standing up in front of a judge...

727
00:53:27,032 --> 00:53:30,033
...while judges and police commissioners are getting blown away.

728
00:53:30,202 --> 00:53:31,994
- what about Dent? - he's got any sense...

729
00:53:32,162 --> 00:53:33,242
...Dent's halfway to mex...

730
00:53:33,414 --> 00:53:34,991
So where do you keep your trash?

731
00:53:36,333 --> 00:53:37,386
You're due in court.

732
00:53:37,387 --> 00:53:40,283
I need you alive long enough to get you on the record

733
00:53:40,462 --> 00:53:43,499
You can't protect me. you can't even protect yourselves.

734
00:53:43,674 --> 00:53:47,007
You refuse to cooperate, you're not coming back here, you go to county.

735
00:53:47,177 --> 00:53:49,633
How long do you calculate you'll last in there?

736
00:53:51,056 --> 00:53:52,551
Targeting me won't get their money.

737
00:53:52,725 --> 00:53:54,551
I knew the mob wouldn't go down easily...

738
00:53:54,727 --> 00:53:56,803
...but this is different. they crossed a line.

739
00:53:56,979 --> 00:53:58,224
You crossed the line first.

740
00:53:58,397 --> 00:54:01,813
You squeezed them, you hammered them to the point of desperation.

741
00:54:01,984 --> 00:54:03,627
And in their desperation,

742
00:54:03,628 --> 00:54:06,978
They turned to a man they didn't fully understand

743
00:54:07,489 --> 00:54:10,027
Criminals aren't complicated, Alfred.

744
00:54:10,200 --> 00:54:12,407
We just need to figure out what he's after.

745
00:54:12,578 --> 00:54:13,989
With respect, master Wayne...

746
00:54:14,163 --> 00:54:17,117
...perhaps this is a man you don't fully understand either.

747
00:54:17,917 --> 00:54:20,621
A long time ago, I was in burma...

748
00:54:20,794 --> 00:54:24,210
...and my friends and I were working for the local government.

749
00:54:24,381 --> 00:54:26,955
They were trying to buy the loyalty of tribal leaders...

750
00:54:27,134 --> 00:54:29,969
...by bribing them with precious stones...

751
00:54:30,137 --> 00:54:32,341
...but their caravans were being raided

752
00:54:32,342 --> 00:54:34,716
In a forest north of rangoon by a bandit

753
00:54:34,892 --> 00:54:38,177
So we went looking for the stones.

754
00:54:38,562 --> 00:54:43,687
But in six months, we never met anyone who traded with him.

755
00:54:44,318 --> 00:54:48,316
One day, I saw a child playing with a ruby...

756
00:54:48,489 --> 00:54:51,525
...the size of a tangerine.

757
00:54:51,784 --> 00:54:55,153
The bandit had been throwing them away.

758
00:54:55,829 --> 00:54:58,534
- so why steal them? - because he thought it was good sport.

759
00:54:58,707 --> 00:55:03,665
Because some men aren't looking for anything logical, like money.

760
00:55:03,837 --> 00:55:08,084
They can't be bought, bullied, reasoned or negotiated with.

761
00:55:08,509 --> 00:55:12,341
Some men just wanna watch the world burn.

762
00:55:32,783 --> 00:55:33,946
Your name, sir?

763
00:55:34,118 --> 00:55:37,284
Eighth and Orchard. you'll find Harvey Dent there.

764
00:55:50,175 --> 00:55:51,634
Check the names.

765
00:55:58,225 --> 00:55:59,933
"richard Dent."

766
00:56:02,146 --> 00:56:03,225
"patrick Harvey."

767
00:56:03,522 --> 00:56:04,553
Harvey Dent.

768
00:56:04,732 --> 00:56:07,733
I need 10 minutes with the scene before your men contaminate it.

769
00:56:07,943 --> 00:56:10,150
It's because of you these guys are dead...

770
00:56:10,321 --> 00:56:11,863
Detective!

771
00:56:14,074 --> 00:56:16,114
Give us a minute, guys.

772
00:56:17,328 --> 00:56:18,905
That's brick underneath.

773
00:56:19,246 --> 00:56:20,906
Gonna take ballistics off a shattered bullet?

774
00:56:21,081 --> 00:56:22,706
No.

775
00:56:24,168 --> 00:56:26,077
Fingerprints.

776
00:56:34,637 --> 00:56:36,546
Whatever you're gonna do, do it fast.

777
00:56:38,349 --> 00:56:43,057
Because we found his next target. he's put it in tomorrow's paper.

778
00:57:00,371 --> 00:57:02,659
I'm not sure you made it loud enough, sir.

779
00:57:15,761 --> 00:57:17,884
What can I do for you, mr. Reese?

780
00:57:18,055 --> 00:57:21,839
You wanted me to do the diligence on the lsi holdings deal again.

781
00:57:22,518 --> 00:57:24,807
Well, I found some irregularities.

782
00:57:25,229 --> 00:57:27,305
Their ceo is in police custody.

783
00:57:27,481 --> 00:57:30,399
No, not with their numbers, with yours.

784
00:57:30,609 --> 00:57:33,694
Applied sciences. whole division of Wayne enterprises...

785
00:57:33,862 --> 00:57:35,522
...just disappeared overnight.

786
00:57:35,698 --> 00:57:39,945
I went down to the archives and I started pulling some old files.

787
00:57:41,078 --> 00:57:42,952
Don't tell me you didn't recognize your baby...

788
00:57:43,122 --> 00:57:46,740
...pancaking cop cars on the evening news.

789
00:57:47,042 --> 00:57:50,246
Now you got the entire r & d department burning through cash...

790
00:57:50,421 --> 00:57:53,754
...claiming it's related to cell phones for the army?

791
00:57:53,924 --> 00:57:57,009
What are you building for him now, a rocket ship?

792
00:57:58,887 --> 00:58:00,631
I want...

793
00:58:00,806 --> 00:58:04,720
...$ 10 million a year for the rest of my life.

794
00:58:07,229 --> 00:58:09,352
Let me get this straight.

795
00:58:10,566 --> 00:58:13,021
You think that your client...

796
00:58:13,193 --> 00:58:16,278
One of the wealthiest, most powerful men in the world...

797
00:58:16,447 --> 00:58:18,024
...is secretly a vigilante...

798
00:58:18,198 --> 00:58:20,188
...who spends his nights beating

799
00:58:20,189 --> 00:58:22,860
Criminals to a pulp with his bare hands..

800
00:58:23,037 --> 00:58:26,203
...and your plan is to blackmail this person?

801
00:58:33,672 --> 00:58:34,953
Good luck.

802
00:58:37,843 --> 00:58:39,254
When...

803
00:58:40,679 --> 00:58:42,138
Keep that.

804
00:58:48,812 --> 00:58:51,268
This is your original scan.

805
00:58:52,691 --> 00:58:54,980
Here it is reengineered.

806
00:59:03,202 --> 00:59:06,737
And there's the thumbprint he left when he pushed the round in the clip.

807
00:59:08,749 --> 00:59:09,912
I'll get you a copy.

808
00:59:10,125 --> 00:59:13,909
Mr. Wayne, did you reassign r & d?

809
00:59:14,088 --> 00:59:16,579
Yeah. government telecommunications project.

810
00:59:16,757 --> 00:59:18,797
Wasn't aware we had any government contracts.

811
00:59:19,051 --> 00:59:22,052
You know, Lucius, I'm playing this one pretty close to the chest.

812
00:59:23,180 --> 00:59:24,888
Fair enough.

813
00:59:27,810 --> 00:59:29,268
With no word from the batman...

814
00:59:29,436 --> 00:59:30,931
...even as they mourn commissioner loeb...

815
00:59:31,105 --> 00:59:34,474
...these cops have to wonder if the Joker will make good on his threat...

816
00:59:34,650 --> 00:59:37,853
...in the obituary column of the Gotham times to kill the mayor.

817
00:59:39,655 --> 00:59:43,320
I've checked all the databases. there are four possibles.

818
00:59:43,492 --> 00:59:45,615
Cross-reference the addresses.

819
00:59:45,786 --> 00:59:49,784
Look for parkside, overlooking the parade.

820
00:59:51,000 --> 00:59:52,114
I got one.

821
00:59:52,293 --> 00:59:56,290
Melvin White, 1502 Randolph apartments.

822
00:59:56,672 --> 01:00:00,752
Aggravated assault, moved to Arkham twice.

823
01:00:39,840 --> 01:00:41,418
What do you got on the roof?

824
01:00:41,592 --> 01:00:45,127
We're tight, but frankly, there's a lot of windows up here.

825
01:00:53,687 --> 01:00:57,732
Commissioner loeb dedicated his life to law enforcement...

826
01:00:57,900 --> 01:01:00,189
...and to the protection of his community.

827
01:01:00,361 --> 01:01:02,152
I remember when I first took office...

828
01:01:02,321 --> 01:01:04,859
...and I asked if he wanted to stay on as commissioner.

829
01:01:05,032 --> 01:01:10,275
And he said he would, provided I kept my politics out of his office.

830
01:01:14,041 --> 01:01:17,208
Clearly he was not a man who minced words, nor should he have been.

831
01:01:18,379 --> 01:01:21,878
A number of policies that he enacted as commissioner were unpopular.

832
01:01:22,049 --> 01:01:25,299
Policies that flooded my office with angry calls and letters...

833
01:01:29,682 --> 01:01:31,342
- who's that? - what happened?

834
01:01:32,393 --> 01:01:34,266
They took our guns.

835
01:01:34,436 --> 01:01:36,228
And our uniforms.

836
01:01:42,820 --> 01:01:45,571
And as we recognize the sacrifice of this man...

837
01:01:45,739 --> 01:01:49,689
...we must remember that vigilance is the price of safety.

838
01:01:49,868 --> 01:01:52,359
Stand by. honor guard.

839
01:01:52,538 --> 01:01:56,156
Attention. port arms.

840
01:01:57,376 --> 01:02:01,753
Ready! aim! fire!

841
01:02:02,548 --> 01:02:04,090
Ready! aim!

842
01:02:07,720 --> 01:02:10,092
Ready! aim!

843
01:02:18,522 --> 01:02:19,933
Stay down! don't move!

844
01:02:21,775 --> 01:02:23,435
Mr. mayor. get him out of here.

845
01:02:32,661 --> 01:02:34,903
- I'll see you later. - why are you going back?

846
01:02:47,551 --> 01:02:48,582
Get out of here.

847
01:02:52,640 --> 01:02:54,383
Tell me what you know about the Joker.

848
01:03:25,422 --> 01:03:26,751
No.

849
01:03:27,174 --> 01:03:28,503
I'm sorry, Barbara.

850
01:03:29,426 --> 01:03:32,676
Jimmy, go play with your sister. go ahead, honey.

851
01:03:32,846 --> 01:03:35,088
If there's anything we can do, anything you need...

852
01:03:35,266 --> 01:03:37,009
...we're here for you.

853
01:03:40,688 --> 01:03:41,933
Are you out there?

854
01:03:43,274 --> 01:03:47,770
Are you? you brought this craziness on us. you did!

855
01:03:47,945 --> 01:03:50,317
You brought this on us!

856
01:03:51,365 --> 01:03:55,943
Switch it off, he ain't coming. he doesn't wanna talk to us.

857
01:03:56,370 --> 01:03:59,371
God help whoever he does wanna talk to.

858
01:04:01,041 --> 01:04:03,959
Can't we go someplace quieter? we can't hear each other talk.

859
01:04:04,128 --> 01:04:06,963
What makes you think I wanna hear you talk?

860
01:04:07,131 --> 01:04:08,162
What?

861
01:04:37,578 --> 01:04:39,202
- yeah? second.

862
01:04:39,371 --> 01:04:40,403
Okay.

863
01:04:40,581 --> 01:04:42,739
- Harvey, where are you? where are you?

864
01:04:42,917 --> 01:04:45,039
I'm where you should be, at major crimes.

865
01:04:45,210 --> 01:04:46,753
I'm trying to deal with all of this mess.

866
01:04:46,921 --> 01:04:48,620
- can I get the fingerprint analysis?

867
01:04:48,621 --> 01:04:50,503
- Rachel, listen to me. you're not safe there

868
01:04:50,674 --> 01:04:52,466
- this is Gordon's unit. - Gordon's gone.

869
01:04:52,635 --> 01:04:56,217
He vouched for these men. - and he's gone.

870
01:05:00,851 --> 01:05:02,927
The Joker's named you next.

871
01:05:03,103 --> 01:05:06,104
God, is there someone, is there anyone in this town we can trust?

872
01:05:06,273 --> 01:05:07,981
Bruce.

873
01:05:08,275 --> 01:05:09,438
We can trust Bruce Wayne.

874
01:05:09,610 --> 01:05:11,187
No. Rachel, I know you're his friend, but...

875
01:05:11,362 --> 01:05:13,188
Harvey, trust me.

876
01:05:13,364 --> 01:05:16,115
Bruce's penthouse is now the safest place in the city.

877
01:05:16,283 --> 01:05:17,612
Then you go straight there.

878
01:05:17,785 --> 01:05:19,908
Don't tell anybody and I'll find you there.

879
01:05:20,079 --> 01:05:21,787
I love you.

880
01:05:35,803 --> 01:05:37,048
I want the Joker.

881
01:05:38,264 --> 01:05:39,924
From one professional to another...

882
01:05:40,099 --> 01:05:42,637
...you're trying to scare somebody, pick a better spot.

883
01:05:42,810 --> 01:05:45,383
From this height, the fall wouldn't kill me.

884
01:05:45,562 --> 01:05:47,140
- I'm counting on it. - huh!

885
01:05:54,530 --> 01:05:57,650
- where is he? - I don't know where he is. he found us.

886
01:05:57,825 --> 01:05:59,105
He must have friends.

887
01:05:59,451 --> 01:06:01,740
Friends? have you met this guy?

888
01:06:01,912 --> 01:06:03,490
Someone knows where he is.

889
01:06:03,664 --> 01:06:06,155
Nobody's gonna tell you nothing.

890
01:06:06,333 --> 01:06:07,662
They're wise to your act.

891
01:06:07,835 --> 01:06:11,833
You got rules. the Joker, he's got no rules.

892
01:06:12,006 --> 01:06:16,881
Nobody's gonna cross him for you. if you want this guy, you got one way.

893
01:06:17,052 --> 01:06:18,844
But you already know what that is.

894
01:06:19,013 --> 01:06:21,800
Just take off that mask, let him come find you.

895
01:06:23,434 --> 01:06:25,338
Or you can let a couple more people

896
01:06:25,339 --> 01:06:27,514
Get killed while you make up your mind

897
01:06:29,189 --> 01:06:31,182
You wanna play games?

898
01:06:37,489 --> 01:06:38,521
How's that feel?

899
01:06:38,699 --> 01:06:41,320
- you wouldn't. - I wouldn't!

900
01:06:42,828 --> 01:06:44,453
- you don't think I will? - mm-mm.

901
01:06:44,622 --> 01:06:46,661
- you don't think I will? - mm-mm.

902
01:06:48,042 --> 01:06:51,245
No. no, I wouldn't.

903
01:06:52,463 --> 01:06:55,001
That's why I'm not gonna leave it up to me.

904
01:06:56,008 --> 01:06:59,009
Heads, you get to keep your head.

905
01:06:59,428 --> 01:07:01,053
Tails...

906
01:07:02,014 --> 01:07:03,045
...not so lucky.

907
01:07:03,432 --> 01:07:06,967
So you wanna tell me about the Joker?

908
01:07:16,362 --> 01:07:20,062
- let's go again. - I don't know anything! god, don't!

909
01:07:20,240 --> 01:07:22,613
You're not playing the odds, friend.

910
01:07:23,744 --> 01:07:25,737
Let's do it again.

911
01:07:28,582 --> 01:07:30,409
You'd leave a man's life to chance?

912
01:07:31,168 --> 01:07:34,751
- not exactly. - his name's Schiff, Thomas.

913
01:07:34,922 --> 01:07:37,923
He's a paranoid schizophrenic, former patient at Arkham.

914
01:07:38,092 --> 01:07:42,718
The kind of mind the Joker attracts. what do you expect to learn from him?

915
01:07:46,058 --> 01:07:48,845
The Joker killed Gordon. he's gonna kill Rachel.

916
01:07:49,019 --> 01:07:51,806
You're the symbol of hope I could never be.

917
01:07:51,981 --> 01:07:53,807
Your stand against organized crime...

918
01:07:53,983 --> 01:07:57,186
...is the first legitimate ray of light in Gotham in decades.

919
01:07:57,361 --> 01:08:00,979
If anyone saw this, everything would be undone.

920
01:08:01,156 --> 01:08:03,445
The criminals you arrested would be released...

921
01:08:03,617 --> 01:08:06,702
...and Jim Gordon will have died for nothing.

922
01:08:07,329 --> 01:08:09,571
You're gonna hold a press conference tomorrow.

923
01:08:09,748 --> 01:08:12,121
- why? - no one else will die because of me.

924
01:08:12,293 --> 01:08:14,618
Gotham's in your hands now.

925
01:08:14,795 --> 01:08:16,503
You can't.

926
01:08:16,672 --> 01:08:18,047
You can't give in.

927
01:08:18,340 --> 01:08:20,878
You can't give in!

928
01:08:36,233 --> 01:08:37,478
Harvey called.

929
01:08:37,651 --> 01:08:40,688
He said batman's gonna turn himself in.

930
01:08:40,863 --> 01:08:41,977
I have no choice.

931
01:08:42,156 --> 01:08:45,240
You honestly think that's gonna keep the Joker from killing people?

932
01:08:45,409 --> 01:08:48,860
Maybe not. but I have enough blood on my hands.

933
01:08:49,330 --> 01:08:54,157
And I've seen now what I would have to become to stop men like him.

934
01:08:54,710 --> 01:08:58,161
You once told me that if the day came when I was finished...

935
01:08:58,339 --> 01:09:00,415
...that we'd be together.

936
01:09:01,133 --> 01:09:04,300
Bruce, don't make me your one hope for a normal life.

937
01:09:05,846 --> 01:09:07,175
Did you mean it?

938
01:09:08,682 --> 01:09:10,509
Yes.

939
01:09:27,785 --> 01:09:29,576
Bruce.

940
01:09:30,537 --> 01:09:34,452
If you turn yourself in, they're not gonna let us be together.

941
01:09:45,094 --> 01:09:48,048
Logs as well? everything.

942
01:09:48,222 --> 01:09:51,591
Anything that could lead back to Lucius or Rachel.

943
01:09:56,939 --> 01:10:00,224
People are dying, Alfred. what would you have me do?

944
01:10:00,401 --> 01:10:04,149
Endure, master Wayne. take it.

945
01:10:04,321 --> 01:10:08,022
They'll hate you for it, but that's the point of batman.

946
01:10:08,200 --> 01:10:13,740
He can be the outcast. he can make the choice that no one else can make.

947
01:10:13,914 --> 01:10:15,243
The right choice.

948
01:10:15,749 --> 01:10:18,786
No, today I found out what batman can't do.

949
01:10:18,961 --> 01:10:20,206
He can't endure this.

950
01:10:20,504 --> 01:10:23,375
Today you get to say "i told you so."

951
01:10:23,966 --> 01:10:27,133
Today, I don't want to.

952
01:10:32,975 --> 01:10:34,434
But I did bloody tell you.

953
01:10:37,479 --> 01:10:40,480
I suppose they're gonna lock me up as well...

954
01:10:41,275 --> 01:10:42,520
...as your accomplice.

955
01:10:42,693 --> 01:10:47,438
Accomplice? I'm gonna tell them the whole thing was your idea.

956
01:10:51,702 --> 01:10:55,237
Ladies and gentlemen, I've called this press conference for two reasons.

957
01:10:55,414 --> 01:10:57,454
Firstly, to assure the citizens of Gotham...

958
01:10:57,625 --> 01:11:01,290
...that everything that can be done over the Joker killings is being done.

959
01:11:02,671 --> 01:11:05,756
Secondly, because the batman has offered to turn himself in.

960
01:11:05,925 --> 01:11:07,632
But let's consider the situation.

961
01:11:08,010 --> 01:11:10,631
Should we give in to this terrorist's demands?

962
01:11:10,804 --> 01:11:12,263
Do we really think he's gonna...?

963
01:11:12,431 --> 01:11:15,800
You'd rather protect an outlaw vigilante than the lives of citizens?

964
01:11:15,976 --> 01:11:18,348
The batman is an outlaw.

965
01:11:19,229 --> 01:11:21,139
That's not why we demand he turn himself in...

966
01:11:21,315 --> 01:11:22,975
...we're doing it because we're scared.

967
01:11:23,150 --> 01:11:25,937
We've been happy to let batman clean up our streets till now.

968
01:11:26,111 --> 01:11:29,065
Things are worse than ever! amen.

969
01:11:30,407 --> 01:11:32,317
Yes, they are.

970
01:11:34,828 --> 01:11:37,829
But the night is darkest just before the dawn.

971
01:11:40,292 --> 01:11:42,368
And I promise you...

972
01:11:43,170 --> 01:11:44,581
...the dawn is coming.

973
01:11:44,755 --> 01:11:46,618
One day, the batman will have to

974
01:11:46,619 --> 01:11:49,298
Answer for the laws he's broken. but to us..

975
01:11:49,468 --> 01:11:51,211
...not to this madman.

976
01:11:51,387 --> 01:11:53,712
- no more dead cops! yeah!

977
01:11:57,017 --> 01:11:58,595
He should turn himself in!

978
01:11:58,769 --> 01:12:01,474
Give us the batman! come on! where is he?

979
01:12:04,358 --> 01:12:06,516
So be it. take the batman into custody.

980
01:12:06,986 --> 01:12:08,943
What? is he here?

981
01:12:09,655 --> 01:12:10,686
I am the batman.

982
01:12:11,031 --> 01:12:14,032
What? come on.

983
01:12:22,418 --> 01:12:24,327
Alfred.

984
01:12:25,671 --> 01:12:27,462
Why is he letting Harvey do this?

985
01:12:27,631 --> 01:12:30,632
- he went down to the press conference. - I know. he just stood by.

986
01:12:30,801 --> 01:12:32,877
Perhaps both Bruce and mr. Dent...

987
01:12:33,053 --> 01:12:36,054
...believe that batman stands for something more important...

988
01:12:36,223 --> 01:12:38,548
...than the whims of a terrorist, miss Dawes...

989
01:12:38,726 --> 01:12:40,718
...even if everyone hates him for it.

990
01:12:40,894 --> 01:12:43,017
That's the sacrifice he's making.

991
01:12:43,188 --> 01:12:46,807
He's not being a hero. he's being something more.

992
01:12:47,359 --> 01:12:48,984
Yeah, you're absolutely right.

993
01:12:49,153 --> 01:12:52,237
Letting Harvey take the fall for this is not heroic at all.

994
01:12:54,908 --> 01:12:56,533
You know him better than anyone.

995
01:12:56,952 --> 01:12:57,983
I do.

996
01:13:01,373 --> 01:13:04,410
Will you give this to him for me? when the time is right?

997
01:13:05,878 --> 01:13:07,076
How will I know?

998
01:13:07,254 --> 01:13:08,748
It's not sealed.

999
01:13:10,174 --> 01:13:11,716
Goodbye, Alfred.

1000
01:13:15,888 --> 01:13:17,631
Bye, Rachel.

1001
01:13:25,522 --> 01:13:27,349
I didn't have time to talk this through.

1002
01:13:27,524 --> 01:13:28,769
What are you doing?

1003
01:13:28,943 --> 01:13:31,019
They're transferring me to central holding.

1004
01:13:31,320 --> 01:13:32,572
This is the Joker's chance,

1005
01:13:32,573 --> 01:13:34,985
And when he attacks, the batman will take him down

1006
01:13:35,157 --> 01:13:36,699
Listen. this is too dangerous.

1007
01:13:36,867 --> 01:13:38,116
We get this guy to county,

1008
01:13:38,117 --> 01:13:40,568
He's their problem. the streets will be cleared..

1009
01:13:40,746 --> 01:13:44,447
...so let's go. the convoys stop for no reason.

1010
01:13:44,625 --> 01:13:46,084
I hope you got some moves, pal.

1011
01:13:46,252 --> 01:13:49,169
He's using you as bait. he doesn't know if he can get the Joker.

1012
01:13:49,338 --> 01:13:50,417
He's failed so far.

1013
01:13:50,756 --> 01:13:52,298
How do you know what he's thinking?

1014
01:13:52,466 --> 01:13:54,791
I just do. anyway, this isn't just about you.

1015
01:13:54,969 --> 01:13:56,795
What about the people depending on you...

1016
01:13:56,971 --> 01:13:59,971
...to clean the city up and do it honorably and...?

1017
01:14:05,646 --> 01:14:08,267
Harvey. tell everyone the truth.

1018
01:14:08,649 --> 01:14:10,523
Heads, I go through with it.

1019
01:14:10,734 --> 01:14:12,644
This is your life. you can't leave...

1020
01:14:12,820 --> 01:14:15,192
...something like that to chance. - I'm not.

1021
01:14:19,535 --> 01:14:21,942
You make your own luck.

1022
01:14:43,767 --> 01:14:45,760
Hey, you wait like everybody else, pal.

1023
01:14:53,402 --> 01:14:55,727
What the hell is that?

1024
01:14:55,904 --> 01:14:58,111
Obstruction ahead, obstruction ahead!

1025
01:14:58,282 --> 01:15:01,485
Damn it! all units divert down onto lower fifth. I repeat, exit down.

1026
01:15:01,911 --> 01:15:03,025
Exit down!

1027
01:15:03,203 --> 01:15:05,529
Lower fifth? we'll be like turkeys on thanksgiving.

1028
01:15:38,238 --> 01:15:40,564
Jesus. come on, get us out of here. let's go.

1029
01:15:42,743 --> 01:15:45,115
Listen, we need backup. we've got company.

1030
01:15:45,287 --> 01:15:46,829
We got trouble, guys.

1031
01:15:49,750 --> 01:15:50,829
Lock and load!

1032
01:16:02,054 --> 01:16:03,429
The hell was that?

1033
01:16:25,286 --> 01:16:27,955
- these are built for that, right? - he'll need something...

1034
01:16:28,122 --> 01:16:29,913
...a lot bigger to get through this.

1035
01:16:30,958 --> 01:16:32,417
What is that?

1036
01:16:33,752 --> 01:16:35,081
What is that, a bazooka?

1037
01:16:43,721 --> 01:16:45,429
I didn't sign up for this!

1038
01:17:01,780 --> 01:17:03,109
Look out.

1039
01:17:03,907 --> 01:17:05,070
Look out!

1040
01:17:27,348 --> 01:17:28,462
Come on, let's go!

1041
01:18:15,113 --> 01:18:17,319
Harvey, Harvey, Harvey Dent.

1042
01:18:17,490 --> 01:18:20,326
Oh, excuse me. I wanna drive.

1043
01:18:25,248 --> 01:18:28,831
Scanning all systems. scanning all systems.

1044
01:18:36,301 --> 01:18:38,424
We gotta get topside. we need air support, now!

1045
01:18:43,933 --> 01:18:45,807
I like this job. I like it.

1046
01:18:48,063 --> 01:18:50,684
Damage catastrophic. eject sequence initiated.

1047
01:19:04,663 --> 01:19:06,157
Goodbye.

1048
01:19:15,256 --> 01:19:18,460
We're on point, ready to give them some of their own medicine.

1049
01:19:24,849 --> 01:19:27,305
That's what I'm talking about. air cav.

1050
01:19:40,865 --> 01:19:42,573
Okay, rack them up.

1051
01:19:42,742 --> 01:19:45,114
Rack them up, rack them up, rack them up.

1052
01:20:10,854 --> 01:20:12,016
That's not good.

1053
01:20:15,525 --> 01:20:16,723
Okay, that's not good!

1054
01:20:59,861 --> 01:21:01,937
Now, there's a batman.

1055
01:21:06,242 --> 01:21:07,441
Ooh, you wanna play. come on.

1056
01:21:10,372 --> 01:21:11,486
Come on.

1057
01:21:20,632 --> 01:21:21,877
He missed!

1058
01:21:35,814 --> 01:21:38,221
You can't stop here. we're like sitting ducks!

1059
01:21:55,250 --> 01:21:56,329
Come on, come on.

1060
01:21:59,462 --> 01:22:02,831
Come on. come on. I want you to do it, I want you to do it. come on!

1061
01:22:05,385 --> 01:22:06,844
Come on.

1062
01:22:07,512 --> 01:22:10,846
Come on. I want you to do it, I want you to do it. come on, hit me.

1063
01:22:11,016 --> 01:22:12,640
Come on, hit me. come on, hit me!

1064
01:22:14,769 --> 01:22:15,801
Hit me!

1065
01:22:44,215 --> 01:22:46,457
Could you please just give me a minute?

1066
01:22:48,553 --> 01:22:50,380
We got you, you son of a bitch.

1067
01:22:53,683 --> 01:22:57,598
Gor... you do like to play things pretty close to the chest.

1068
01:22:58,063 --> 01:22:59,771
We got him, Harvey.

1069
01:22:59,939 --> 01:23:03,391
Mr. Dent! how does it feel to be the biggest hero in Gotham?

1070
01:23:03,568 --> 01:23:06,854
No, I'm no hero. Gotham's finest, they're the heroes.

1071
01:23:07,030 --> 01:23:08,358
But you and your office...

1072
01:23:08,531 --> 01:23:10,191
...have been working with the batman all along.

1073
01:23:10,367 --> 01:23:12,158
No, but I trusted him to do the right thing.

1074
01:23:12,327 --> 01:23:14,403
Which was? - saving my ass.

1075
01:23:14,579 --> 01:23:17,497
All right, people, that's enough. let him be. let him be.

1076
01:23:17,666 --> 01:23:19,575
Thank you, detective.

1077
01:23:19,793 --> 01:23:21,916
I've got a date with a pretty upset girlfriend.

1078
01:23:22,087 --> 01:23:24,459
- I figured, counselor. mr. Dent, sir...

1079
01:23:24,631 --> 01:23:28,759
...how about one for the front page, sir? mr. Dent.

1080
01:23:40,105 --> 01:23:43,271
Stand away! all of you!

1081
01:23:43,441 --> 01:23:46,941
I don't want anything for his mob lawyer to use, you understand?

1082
01:23:49,197 --> 01:23:51,071
Back from the dead.

1083
01:23:51,741 --> 01:23:53,283
I, uh...

1084
01:23:53,451 --> 01:23:55,361
...couldn't risk my family's safety.

1085
01:23:56,663 --> 01:23:58,490
What do we got?

1086
01:24:00,166 --> 01:24:04,116
Nothing. no matches on prints, dna, Dental.

1087
01:24:04,296 --> 01:24:07,047
Clothing is custom, no labels.

1088
01:24:07,257 --> 01:24:09,380
Nothing in his pockets but knives and lint.

1089
01:24:09,551 --> 01:24:11,460
No name.

1090
01:24:11,803 --> 01:24:13,760
- no other alias. go home, Gordon.

1091
01:24:13,930 --> 01:24:17,014
The clown'll keep till morning. go get some rest.

1092
01:24:17,183 --> 01:24:19,010
You're gonna need it.

1093
01:24:19,269 --> 01:24:21,842
Tomorrow you take the big job.

1094
01:24:22,522 --> 01:24:25,689
You don't have any say in the matter. commissioner Gordon.

1095
01:24:41,541 --> 01:24:43,664
I'm sorry, I couldn't risk your safety.

1096
01:24:50,175 --> 01:24:51,586
Look at these ugly bastards.

1097
01:24:51,760 --> 01:24:53,633
- I don't feel good. you're a cop killer.

1098
01:24:53,803 --> 01:24:56,129
You're lucky to be feeling anything below the neck.

1099
01:24:56,306 --> 01:24:57,883
- please! - step away from the bars!

1100
01:24:58,058 --> 01:25:00,216
My insides hurt.

1101
01:25:14,407 --> 01:25:16,199
Did batman save you, daddy?

1102
01:25:18,370 --> 01:25:20,658
Actually, this time...

1103
01:25:20,830 --> 01:25:22,989
...i saved him.

1104
01:25:34,344 --> 01:25:35,968
Has he said anything yet?

1105
01:25:43,561 --> 01:25:47,773
Evening, commissioner.

1106
01:25:55,407 --> 01:25:57,613
Harvey Dent never made it home.

1107
01:25:57,784 --> 01:25:59,907
- of course not. - what have you done with him?

1108
01:26:00,829 --> 01:26:02,572
Me?

1109
01:26:04,207 --> 01:26:06,330
I was right here.

1110
01:26:07,752 --> 01:26:09,579
Who did you leave him with?

1111
01:26:09,754 --> 01:26:12,589
Hm? your people?

1112
01:26:13,717 --> 01:26:17,050
Assuming, of course, that they are still your people...

1113
01:26:17,220 --> 01:26:19,925
...and not Maroni's.

1114
01:26:22,142 --> 01:26:24,514
Does it depress you, commissioner...

1115
01:26:24,936 --> 01:26:29,894
...to know just how alone you really are?

1116
01:26:31,901 --> 01:26:36,777
Does it make you feel responsible for Harvey Dent's current predicament?

1117
01:26:36,948 --> 01:26:39,618
- where is he? - what's the time?

1118
01:26:40,118 --> 01:26:41,612
What difference does that make?

1119
01:26:41,870 --> 01:26:47,326
Well, depending on the time, he may be in one spot or several.

1120
01:26:53,715 --> 01:26:56,669
- lf we're gonna play games... - mm-hm?

1121
01:26:59,846 --> 01:27:01,803
...i'm gonna need a cup of coffee.

1122
01:27:01,973 --> 01:27:06,053
Ah, the "good cop, bad cop" routine?

1123
01:27:06,728 --> 01:27:07,759
Not exactly.

1124
01:27:18,281 --> 01:27:19,613
Never start with the head.

1125
01:27:19,614 --> 01:27:22,326
The victim gets all fuzzy. he can't feel the next..

1126
01:27:25,497 --> 01:27:26,611
See?

1127
01:27:26,790 --> 01:27:29,115
You wanted me. here I am.

1128
01:27:30,168 --> 01:27:32,291
I wanted to see what you'd do.

1129
01:27:32,837 --> 01:27:35,411
And you didn't disappoint.

1130
01:27:35,590 --> 01:27:38,425
You let five people die.

1131
01:27:39,386 --> 01:27:43,051
Then you let Dent take your place.

1132
01:27:43,223 --> 01:27:45,844
- even to a guy like me, that's cold. - where's Dent?

1133
01:27:46,017 --> 01:27:50,810
Those mob fools want you gone so they can get back to the way things were.

1134
01:27:51,314 --> 01:27:56,060
But I know the truth. there's no going back. you've changed things.

1135
01:27:56,236 --> 01:27:58,643
- forever. - then why do you wanna kill me?

1136
01:28:01,616 --> 01:28:03,027
I don't wanna kill you.

1137
01:28:03,535 --> 01:28:08,078
What would I do without you? go back to ripping off mob dealers? no, no.

1138
01:28:08,248 --> 01:28:10,620
No. no, you...

1139
01:28:10,792 --> 01:28:13,200
You complete me.

1140
01:28:13,378 --> 01:28:15,380
- you're garbage who kills for money.

1141
01:28:15,381 --> 01:28:17,707
- don't talk like one of them. you're not

1142
01:28:17,882 --> 01:28:20,290
Even if you'd like to be.

1143
01:28:21,553 --> 01:28:23,380
To them, you're just a freak...

1144
01:28:24,306 --> 01:28:25,634
...like me.

1145
01:28:25,807 --> 01:28:28,096
They need you right now...

1146
01:28:28,685 --> 01:28:30,724
...but when they don't...

1147
01:28:31,271 --> 01:28:34,307
...they'll cast you out like a leper.

1148
01:28:34,482 --> 01:28:38,397
You see, their morals, their code...

1149
01:28:38,653 --> 01:28:40,812
...it's a bad joke.

1150
01:28:41,072 --> 01:28:44,406
Dropped at the first sign of trouble.

1151
01:28:45,076 --> 01:28:49,074
They're only as good as the world allows them to be. I'll show you.

1152
01:28:49,247 --> 01:28:52,414
When the chips are down, these...

1153
01:28:52,584 --> 01:28:54,826
These civilized people...

1154
01:28:55,003 --> 01:28:57,079
...they'll eat each other.

1155
01:28:57,797 --> 01:29:00,170
See, I'm not a monster.

1156
01:29:01,551 --> 01:29:02,832
I'm just ahead of the curve.

1157
01:29:05,096 --> 01:29:06,176
Where's Dent?

1158
01:29:06,348 --> 01:29:09,265
You have all these rules, and you think they'll save you.

1159
01:29:12,354 --> 01:29:14,761
- he's in control. - I have one rule.

1160
01:29:14,939 --> 01:29:18,024
Oh. then that's the rule you'll have to break to know the truth.

1161
01:29:18,193 --> 01:29:19,355
Which is?

1162
01:29:19,527 --> 01:29:21,935
The only sensible way to live is without rules.

1163
01:29:22,113 --> 01:29:24,783
And tonight you're gonna break your one rule.

1164
01:29:24,950 --> 01:29:25,981
I'm considering it.

1165
01:29:26,159 --> 01:29:28,780
There's only minutes left, so you'll have to play my game...

1166
01:29:28,954 --> 01:29:31,527
...if you wanna save one of them.

1167
01:29:32,040 --> 01:29:33,071
"them"?

1168
01:29:33,249 --> 01:29:37,294
You know, for a while there, I thought you really were Dent.

1169
01:29:37,462 --> 01:29:40,083
The way you threw yourself after her.

1170
01:29:46,388 --> 01:29:47,467
Look at you go.

1171
01:29:53,103 --> 01:29:56,685
Does Harvey know about you and his little bunny?

1172
01:29:57,607 --> 01:29:58,982
Where are they?!

1173
01:29:59,150 --> 01:30:01,143
Killing is making a choice.

1174
01:30:01,319 --> 01:30:04,404
- where are they?! - choose between one life or the other.

1175
01:30:05,156 --> 01:30:09,403
Your friend the district attorney, or his blushing bride-to-be.

1176
01:30:14,582 --> 01:30:18,663
You have nothing, nothing to threaten me with.

1177
01:30:19,087 --> 01:30:22,586
Nothing to do with all your strength.

1178
01:30:22,799 --> 01:30:26,215
Don't worry, I'm gonna tell you where they are, both of them.

1179
01:30:26,386 --> 01:30:29,422
And that's the point. you'll have to choose.

1180
01:30:30,181 --> 01:30:33,017
He's at 2505 2nd street...

1181
01:30:33,184 --> 01:30:36,518
...and she's on avenue x at cicero.

1182
01:30:38,606 --> 01:30:40,350
- which one you going after? - Rachel.

1183
01:30:41,776 --> 01:30:43,187
We're getting Dent!

1184
01:30:45,447 --> 01:30:48,282
2505 2nd street!

1185
01:30:51,202 --> 01:30:53,029
Hello?

1186
01:30:53,997 --> 01:30:56,369
Can anybody hear me?

1187
01:30:58,793 --> 01:31:01,415
Hello!

1188
01:31:05,425 --> 01:31:07,667
- Rachel? - Harvey.

1189
01:31:07,844 --> 01:31:10,050
Oh, Harvey, thank god. are you okay?

1190
01:31:10,221 --> 01:31:11,799
I'm all right. I'm in a...

1191
01:31:11,973 --> 01:31:15,556
I'm in a warehouse.They got me wired to these oil drums.

1192
01:31:16,603 --> 01:31:17,801
I am too.

1193
01:31:18,355 --> 01:31:20,063
Harvey.

1194
01:31:27,322 --> 01:31:29,777
I want my phone call.

1195
01:31:29,950 --> 01:31:32,737
I want it. I want it.I want my phone call.

1196
01:31:33,411 --> 01:31:35,238
That's nice.

1197
01:31:36,748 --> 01:31:41,576
How many of your friends have I killed?

1198
01:31:45,340 --> 01:31:46,419
I'm a 20-year man...

1199
01:31:46,591 --> 01:31:50,043
...and I know the difference between punks who need a lesson in manners...

1200
01:31:50,220 --> 01:31:53,090
...and the freaks like you who would just enjoy it.

1201
01:31:53,974 --> 01:31:56,429
And you killed six of my friends.

1202
01:31:56,601 --> 01:31:57,632
Six?

1203
01:31:57,811 --> 01:32:00,266
Please. My insides hurt.

1204
01:32:00,438 --> 01:32:02,182
I don't really care. Back away.

1205
01:32:02,357 --> 01:32:05,524
The boss said he'd make the voices go away.

1206
01:32:05,694 --> 01:32:09,228
He said he'd go inside and replace them with bright lights...

1207
01:32:09,406 --> 01:32:10,520
...like Christmas.

1208
01:32:10,699 --> 01:32:13,237
You're out of your mind, pal. Back off.

1209
01:32:13,410 --> 01:32:16,245
Medic to the holding tank.Come on. Get the door open.

1210
01:32:16,454 --> 01:32:17,617
You guys, back off!

1211
01:32:17,789 --> 01:32:19,947
Listen, we don't have a lot of time.

1212
01:32:20,125 --> 01:32:24,122
They told me that only one of us was gonna make it...

1213
01:32:24,296 --> 01:32:27,629
...and that they were gonna let our friends choose.

1214
01:32:30,343 --> 01:32:32,466
Okay, Rachel.

1215
01:32:33,054 --> 01:32:36,174
It's gonna be fine. It's gonna be all right.They're coming for you.

1216
01:32:36,349 --> 01:32:40,643
Listen to me. I'll help you. Just talk me through what's going on with you.

1217
01:32:40,812 --> 01:32:42,721
Can you find something,anything, sharp?

1218
01:32:42,897 --> 01:32:44,308
I'm trying.

1219
01:32:44,482 --> 01:32:46,641
- What's...?- Shit.

1220
01:32:46,818 --> 01:32:48,312
Harvey?

1221
01:32:52,073 --> 01:32:53,733
Harvey, what's happening?

1222
01:33:03,084 --> 01:33:06,916
All available units, converge at 2505 2nd Street.

1223
01:33:07,255 --> 01:33:11,335
Do you wanna know why I use a knife?

1224
01:33:13,637 --> 01:33:14,965
Guns are too quick.

1225
01:33:15,138 --> 01:33:18,507
You can't savor all the...

1226
01:33:18,683 --> 01:33:22,017
...little emotions.

1227
01:33:23,938 --> 01:33:28,814
You see, in their last moments...

1228
01:33:28,985 --> 01:33:31,274
...people show you who they really are.

1229
01:33:32,364 --> 01:33:38,034
So in a way, I knew your friends better than you ever did.

1230
01:33:41,790 --> 01:33:45,206
Would you like to know which of them were cowards?

1231
01:33:51,716 --> 01:33:53,376
What's that? Jeez.

1232
01:33:53,593 --> 01:33:55,633
He's got some kind of a...

1233
01:33:55,804 --> 01:33:59,007
...contusion.- I know you're gonna enjoy this.

1234
01:34:00,392 --> 01:34:04,140
I'm gonna have to try and enjoy it even more.

1235
01:34:11,695 --> 01:34:12,726
Just put it down.

1236
01:34:12,904 --> 01:34:15,691
Take it easy. Take it easy. Drop the weapon now!

1237
01:34:15,865 --> 01:34:19,815
- It's my own damn fault, just shoot him!- Let him go now! Drop it!

1238
01:34:20,120 --> 01:34:23,121
- What? Sorry?- What do you want?

1239
01:34:24,165 --> 01:34:26,075
I just want my phone call.

1240
01:34:29,087 --> 01:34:31,756
What...? What...? What's happening?

1241
01:34:31,923 --> 01:34:34,758
Just talk to me, just for one second.

1242
01:34:37,095 --> 01:34:39,764
- All right?- Right.

1243
01:34:51,568 --> 01:34:53,607
Is that a phone?

1244
01:35:03,288 --> 01:35:04,616
Mount the curb!

1245
01:35:12,631 --> 01:35:16,628
Harvey, just in case, I wanna tell you something, okay?

1246
01:35:16,801 --> 01:35:18,593
Don't think like that. They're coming.

1247
01:35:18,762 --> 01:35:21,050
I know they are,but I don't want them to.

1248
01:35:25,477 --> 01:35:29,557
I don't wanna live without you,and I do have an answer for you.

1249
01:35:29,981 --> 01:35:31,725
My answer is yes.

1250
01:35:34,486 --> 01:35:37,237
No! No! No!

1251
01:35:37,405 --> 01:35:40,027
Not me! Why are you coming for me?

1252
01:35:40,200 --> 01:35:41,231
No!

1253
01:35:42,911 --> 01:35:44,488
Rachel! Rachel!

1254
01:35:44,704 --> 01:35:47,030
- Harvey.- No! No! Rachel!

1255
01:35:47,207 --> 01:35:48,238
Okay.

1256
01:35:48,416 --> 01:35:49,496
Rachel!

1257
01:35:49,918 --> 01:35:51,460
No! No!

1258
01:35:51,628 --> 01:35:55,756
Harvey, it's okay. It's all right. Listen.

1259
01:35:55,924 --> 01:35:57,252
Somewh...

1260
01:36:03,139 --> 01:36:04,337
No, commissioner!

1261
01:36:04,516 --> 01:36:07,185
Rachel! No!

1262
01:36:21,533 --> 01:36:22,647
Hello there.

1263
01:36:28,540 --> 01:36:32,039
Back at the MCU, the Joker's gone.

1264
01:36:32,961 --> 01:36:34,669
With Lau?

