Jesus. I thought you was dead.

1517
01:55:11,871 --> 01:55:13,531
Half.

1518
01:55:19,587 --> 01:55:21,165
Who picked up Rachel, Wuertz?

1519
01:55:21,339 --> 01:55:23,332
- it must've been Maroni's men. - shut up!

1520
01:55:25,093 --> 01:55:27,216
Are you telling me that you're gonna protect...

1521
01:55:27,387 --> 01:55:29,130
...the other traitor in Gordon's unit?

1522
01:55:29,306 --> 01:55:30,764
I don't know, he never told me.

1523
01:55:30,932 --> 01:55:32,331
Listen, Dent, I swear to god,

1524
01:55:32,333 --> 01:55:34,550
I didn't know what they were gonna do to you

1525
01:55:36,104 --> 01:55:37,267
That's funny...

1526
01:55:39,024 --> 01:55:41,775
...because I don't know what's gonna happen to you either.

1527
01:55:45,905 --> 01:55:47,815
Beautiful, isn't it?

1528
01:55:48,199 --> 01:55:49,859
Beautiful.

1529
01:55:50,410 --> 01:55:51,525
Unethical.

1530
01:55:52,704 --> 01:55:54,246
Dangerous.

1531
01:55:54,456 --> 01:55:57,955
You've turned every cell phone in Gotham into a microphone.

1532
01:55:58,126 --> 01:56:00,534
And a high-frequency generator-receiver.

1533
01:56:00,712 --> 01:56:05,789
You took my sonar concept and applied it to every phone in the city.

1534
01:56:05,967 --> 01:56:10,546
With half the city feeding you sonar, you can image all of Gotham.

1535
01:56:12,474 --> 01:56:13,849
This is wrong.

1536
01:56:14,017 --> 01:56:16,056
I've gotta find this man, Lucius.

1537
01:56:18,063 --> 01:56:19,343
At what cost?

1538
01:56:19,522 --> 01:56:22,310
The database is null-key encrypted.

1539
01:56:22,484 --> 01:56:24,690
It can only be accessed by one person.

1540
01:56:26,029 --> 01:56:28,187
This is too much power for one person.

1541
01:56:28,365 --> 01:56:30,523
That's why I gave it to you.

1542
01:56:30,992 --> 01:56:32,190
Only you can use it.

1543
01:56:32,369 --> 01:56:36,153
Spying on 30 million people isn't part of my job description.

1544
01:56:38,375 --> 01:56:39,528
This is an audio Sample.

1545
01:56:39,529 --> 01:56:42,075
If he talks within range of any phone in the city..

1546
01:56:42,253 --> 01:56:44,460
...you can triangulate his position.

1547
01:56:44,923 --> 01:56:47,414
I'll help you this one time.

1548
01:56:47,884 --> 01:56:49,675
But consider this my resignation.

1549
01:56:49,844 --> 01:56:54,423
As long as this machine is at Wayne enterprises, I won't be.

1550
01:56:55,183 --> 01:56:57,092
When you're finished...

1551
01:56:57,769 --> 01:56:58,884
...type in your name.

1552
01:57:07,487 --> 01:57:10,571
My officers are going over every inch of the tunnels and bridges...

1553
01:57:10,740 --> 01:57:13,943
...but with the Joker's threat, they're not an option.

1554
01:57:14,119 --> 01:57:16,954
- and land routes east? - backed up for hours.

1555
01:57:17,122 --> 01:57:20,740
Which leaves the ferries with 30,000 ready to board.

1556
01:57:20,917 --> 01:57:23,954
I wanna use the ferries so I can get those prisoners off the island.

1557
01:57:24,296 --> 01:57:27,083
The men you put away? those aren't people I'm worried about.

1558
01:57:27,257 --> 01:57:29,380
You should be. whatever the Joker's planning...

1559
01:57:29,551 --> 01:57:31,605
...it's a good bet Harvey's prisoners

1560
01:57:31,606 --> 01:57:34,047
Are involved. I wanna get them out of here

1561
01:57:35,515 --> 01:57:36,713
So where is Harvey?

1562
01:57:37,309 --> 01:57:40,475
- we haven't found him. - oh, jesus.

1563
01:57:44,316 --> 01:57:46,392
How long can you keep this quiet?

1564
01:58:00,498 --> 01:58:03,168
Don't stop for lights, cops, nothing.

1565
01:58:04,002 --> 01:58:06,160
Going to join your wife?

1566
01:58:09,674 --> 01:58:12,165
- you love her? - yes.

1567
01:58:13,053 --> 01:58:16,007
You ever imagine what it would be like to listen to her die?

1568
01:58:16,181 --> 01:58:17,675
Look, take it up with the Joker.

1569
01:58:17,849 --> 01:58:21,099
He killed your woman. he made you...

1570
01:58:21,269 --> 01:58:22,300
...like this.

1571
01:58:22,687 --> 01:58:25,688
The Joker's just a mad dog.

1572
01:58:25,857 --> 01:58:28,478
I want whoever let him off the leash.

1573
01:58:29,194 --> 01:58:32,527
I took care of Wuertz, but who was your other man inside Gordon's unit?

1574
01:58:32,697 --> 01:58:35,319
Who picked up Rachel? must have been someone she trusted.

1575
01:58:36,534 --> 01:58:38,657
Look, if I tell you...

1576
01:58:38,828 --> 01:58:39,860
...will you let me go?

1577
01:58:40,622 --> 01:58:41,950
Can't hurt your chances.

1578
01:58:44,709 --> 01:58:46,369
It was Ramirez.

1579
01:58:51,800 --> 01:58:55,050
- but you said... - I said it couldn't hurt your chances.

1580
01:58:58,640 --> 01:59:00,763
You're a lucky man.

1581
01:59:04,229 --> 01:59:05,972
- but he's not. - who?

1582
01:59:08,900 --> 01:59:10,311
Your driver.

1583
01:59:23,540 --> 01:59:24,571
Stand back.

1584
01:59:24,749 --> 01:59:27,075
Hey, that ain't right. we should be on that boat.

1585
01:59:27,252 --> 01:59:29,825
You wanna ride across with them? be my guest.

1586
01:59:53,069 --> 01:59:54,777
Sir, they've stopped their engines.

1587
01:59:54,946 --> 01:59:55,977
Right, get on the radio.

1588
01:59:56,156 --> 01:59:59,774
Tell them we'll come back and pick them up once we dump the scumbags.

1589
01:59:59,951 --> 02:00:02,323
Liberty, this is Spirit. come in.

1590
02:00:04,372 --> 02:00:05,570
What the heck was that?

1591
02:00:07,500 --> 02:00:08,959
What the...?

1592
02:00:09,502 --> 02:00:12,788
Liberty, come in, please. this is Spirit. come in.

1593
02:00:14,424 --> 02:00:16,298
Liberty, we have the Same thing. we've lost both engines.

1594
02:00:16,468 --> 02:00:17,962
- Liberty, come in. Fox.

1595
02:00:18,136 --> 02:00:20,627
There's something going on on the ferries.

1596
02:00:21,389 --> 02:00:23,678
Get down to the engine room now.

1597
02:00:24,309 --> 02:00:26,515
Hey, buddy, what's happening?

1598
02:00:35,111 --> 02:00:38,563
Captain, we got a hundred barrels down there rigged to blow. and this.

1599
02:00:52,921 --> 02:00:54,748
Looks like some kind of detonator.

1600
02:00:54,923 --> 02:00:57,793
Why would they give us the detonator to our own bomb?

1601
02:01:00,720 --> 02:01:02,096
Tonight, you're all gonna...

1602
02:01:02,263 --> 02:01:04,007
... be a part of a social experiment.

1603
02:01:07,852 --> 02:01:11,684
Through the magic of diesel fuel and ammonium nitrate...

1604
02:01:11,856 --> 02:01:15,937
... I'm ready right now to blow you all sky-high.

1605
02:01:16,111 --> 02:01:18,187
Liberty, come in, over.

1606
02:01:19,656 --> 02:01:20,687
It's dead.

1607
02:01:21,032 --> 02:01:25,528
If anyone attempts to get off their boat, you all die.

1608
02:01:25,870 --> 02:01:27,151
I'm zeroing in.

1609
02:01:27,330 --> 02:01:31,873
Each of you has a remote to blow up the other boat.

1610
02:01:32,043 --> 02:01:34,499
His voice is on the ferry...

1611
02:01:34,671 --> 02:01:36,710
...but it's not the source.

1612
02:01:38,967 --> 02:01:40,082
West.

1613
02:01:47,350 --> 02:01:49,639
- Gordon. I have the Joker's location.

1614
02:01:49,811 --> 02:01:50,890
Prewitt building.

1615
02:01:51,062 --> 02:01:53,518
Assemble on the building opposite.

1616
02:01:54,899 --> 02:01:57,687
At midnight, I blow you all up.

1617
02:01:57,861 --> 02:02:03,021
If, however, one of you presses the button, I'll let that boat live.

1618
02:02:03,199 --> 02:02:05,322
So who's it gonna be?

1619
02:02:05,493 --> 02:02:08,031
Harvey Dent's most-wanted scumbag collection...

1620
02:02:08,204 --> 02:02:11,538
... or the sweet and innocent civilians?

1621
02:02:11,708 --> 02:02:14,246
You choose.

1622
02:02:14,419 --> 02:02:16,328
Oh, and you might wanna decide quickly...

1623
02:02:16,504 --> 02:02:20,834
... because the people on the other boat may not be quite so noble.

1624
02:02:28,224 --> 02:02:29,256
Stay back.

1625
02:02:29,434 --> 02:02:33,218
Well, now, who are you to decide? we ought to talk this over, at least.

1626
02:02:33,605 --> 02:02:37,188
We don't all have to die. those men had their chance.

1627
02:02:37,817 --> 02:02:41,601
- we are not going to talk about this. - why aren't we talking about it?

1628
02:02:41,780 --> 02:02:44,353
They're talking over the Same thing on the other boat.

1629
02:02:44,532 --> 02:02:46,821
- let's put it to a vote. yes!

1630
02:02:52,123 --> 02:02:54,697
- hello? Barbara, it's Anna Ramirez.

1631
02:02:54,876 --> 02:02:57,912
Jim needs you to pack up and put the kids in the car right away.

1632
02:02:58,088 --> 02:02:59,796
But the units outside...

1633
02:02:59,965 --> 02:03:01,542
Those cops can't be trusted.

1634
02:03:01,716 --> 02:03:04,670
Jim needs you away from them as soon as possible.

1635
02:03:04,844 --> 02:03:07,798
I'll call them off for 10 minutes, and you'll have to move fast.

1636
02:03:07,973 --> 02:03:11,804
- but where am I supposed to take them? - 2505 2nd street.

1637
02:03:11,977 --> 02:03:13,850
Leave as soon as the patrol car pulls out.

1638
02:03:14,020 --> 02:03:15,396
Okay.

1639
02:03:15,772 --> 02:03:17,563
She believe you?

1640
02:03:17,774 --> 02:03:19,814
It's because she trusts you...

1641
02:03:20,151 --> 02:03:21,231
...just like rachel did.

1642
02:03:21,403 --> 02:03:23,479
- I didn't know... - didn't know what they'd do?

1643
02:03:23,655 --> 02:03:26,407
You're the second cop to say that to me.

1644
02:03:26,658 --> 02:03:28,781
What exactly did you think they were gonna do?

1645
02:03:28,952 --> 02:03:31,194
They got me early on. my mother's hospital bills...

1646
02:03:31,371 --> 02:03:34,407
- don't! - I'm sorry.

1647
02:03:34,958 --> 02:03:37,413
You live to fight another day, officer.

1648
02:03:41,214 --> 02:03:43,041
We found the missing hospital bus.

1649
02:03:43,216 --> 02:03:44,924
Then we have a hostage situation.

1650
02:03:47,012 --> 02:03:49,004
It's a shooting gallery.

1651
02:03:49,389 --> 02:03:51,678
Why would he choose a spot with such big windows?

1652
02:03:51,850 --> 02:03:53,677
We have clear shots on five clowns.

1653
02:03:53,852 --> 02:03:56,603
Snipers take them out, smash the windows, a team rappels in.

1654
02:03:57,022 --> 02:03:58,516
Team moves in by the stairwells.

1655
02:03:58,690 --> 02:04:00,813
Two, three casualties max.

1656
02:04:00,984 --> 02:04:02,858
- let's do it. it's not that simple.

1657
02:04:03,028 --> 02:04:05,353
- with the Joker, it never is. - what's simple is...

1658
02:04:05,530 --> 02:04:08,697
...every second, those people on the ferries get closer to blowing...

1659
02:04:08,867 --> 02:04:11,405
- that won't happen. - then he'll blow both of them up!

1660
02:04:11,578 --> 02:04:13,406
- we don't have time for paper ballots.

1661
02:04:13,407 --> 02:04:15,326
- I want everybody to put their votes..

1662
02:04:15,498 --> 02:04:17,491
...on this piece of paper.

1663
02:04:18,543 --> 02:04:21,378
If anyone's got pens, pass it along.

1664
02:04:21,713 --> 02:04:23,504
Thank you. anybody else?

1665
02:04:23,673 --> 02:04:25,500
Coming through. anybody else? thank you.

1666
02:04:25,675 --> 02:04:28,546
We need to get these votes in quickly.

1667
02:04:28,720 --> 02:04:30,262
Come on.

1668
02:04:32,265 --> 02:04:34,388
What are you waiting for? push the button!

1669
02:04:34,559 --> 02:04:36,516
We're running out of time!

1670
02:04:37,812 --> 02:04:39,639
I need five minutes alone.

1671
02:04:39,814 --> 02:04:41,641
No! there's no time!

1672
02:04:41,816 --> 02:04:43,227
We have clear shots!

1673
02:04:43,401 --> 02:04:46,319
Dent is in there with them. we have to save Dent!

1674
02:04:46,488 --> 02:04:48,445
I have to save Dent.

1675
02:04:48,615 --> 02:04:49,729
Get ready.

1676
02:04:52,577 --> 02:04:55,246
Two minutes, then we breach.

1677
02:05:00,835 --> 02:05:02,330
Fox, I need picture.

1678
02:05:05,382 --> 02:05:07,837
- hello? jim, we're in trouble.

1679
02:05:09,094 --> 02:05:11,382
Okay, you got pov on alpha...

1680
02:05:12,430 --> 02:05:14,387
... omni on beta.

1681
02:05:15,850 --> 02:05:19,219
Looks like clowns and hostages on two floors.

1682
02:05:19,396 --> 02:05:21,803
There's a swa t team on the stairwell.

1683
02:05:25,110 --> 02:05:27,731
Another swa t team on the roof.

1684
02:05:29,281 --> 02:05:30,479
Line's clear.

1685
02:05:32,242 --> 02:05:34,947
- barbara, calm down. - he has the kids!

1686
02:05:35,120 --> 02:05:38,370
Hello, jim. - Harvey?

1687
02:05:39,165 --> 02:05:42,369
- where's my family? - where my family died.

1688
02:05:45,463 --> 02:05:47,123
Blue team, acquire the target.

1689
02:05:48,800 --> 02:05:51,373
Entry team, set your charge.

1690
02:06:07,319 --> 02:06:09,145
Fox, the swa ts are targeting the wrong people.

1691
02:06:09,321 --> 02:06:10,815
The clowns are the hostages.

1692
02:06:11,531 --> 02:06:13,322
Red team, go! red team, go!

1693
02:06:17,078 --> 02:06:18,489
Entry team, blow and go!

1694
02:06:22,584 --> 02:06:23,995
Don't move.

1695
02:06:25,170 --> 02:06:26,545
Take the shot.

1696
02:06:32,177 --> 02:06:33,837
Those swats are coming in hot.

1697
02:06:34,012 --> 02:06:35,839
Clowns, put down your guns.

1698
02:06:36,348 --> 02:06:38,969
Drop your weapons! on the ground, now!

1699
02:06:39,184 --> 02:06:42,350
Doctors, get down! clear the line of fire. drop your weap...

1700
02:07:06,962 --> 02:07:08,124
Freeze!

1701
02:07:08,296 --> 02:07:10,668
Stand down or you will be...

1702
02:07:14,219 --> 02:07:15,678
Look up.

1703
02:07:16,262 --> 02:07:18,836
See those bad guys on the floor above?

1704
02:07:19,015 --> 02:07:22,016
They're waiting to ambush the swat team coming up the elevator.

1705
02:07:22,477 --> 02:07:23,508
Sixty seconds.

1706
02:07:31,820 --> 02:07:36,398
The tally is 140 against, 396 for.

1707
02:07:44,541 --> 02:07:47,079
So go ahead. do it.

1708
02:07:47,252 --> 02:07:49,244
We're still here.

1709
02:07:50,422 --> 02:07:53,376
And that means they haven't killed us yet either.

1710
02:07:54,843 --> 02:07:56,586
Go, go, go!

1711
02:07:56,761 --> 02:07:58,553
Blue team, cover!

1712
02:08:04,060 --> 02:08:05,720
Trouble on the floor above.

1713
02:08:15,071 --> 02:08:16,447
Get down on the ground now!

1714
02:08:24,873 --> 02:08:27,280
Freeze! stop or we will shoot.

1715
02:08:27,459 --> 02:08:29,451
We will shoot you. drop the officer.

1716
02:08:29,628 --> 02:08:31,170
Release the officer right now.

1717
02:08:31,338 --> 02:08:33,295
Let him go now! on your knees!

1718
02:08:33,882 --> 02:08:35,958
We got him. he's out of the game.

1719
02:08:36,134 --> 02:08:38,625
Keep your hands in the air! step away from the edge!

1720
02:08:46,686 --> 02:08:48,311
Halt!

1721
02:09:01,618 --> 02:09:02,993
Stay down! don't move!

1722
02:09:03,161 --> 02:09:07,455
Be advised. clowns are hostages, doctors are targets.

1723
02:09:13,755 --> 02:09:15,913
Ah, you made it. I'm so thrilled.

1724
02:09:16,091 --> 02:09:19,257
- where's the detonator? - go get him.

1725
02:09:32,649 --> 02:09:35,733
Put down your weapon! don't move!

1726
02:10:07,142 --> 02:10:09,015
You don't wanna die...

1727
02:10:09,185 --> 02:10:12,222
...but you don't know how to take a life.

1728
02:10:12,397 --> 02:10:14,057
Give it to me.

1729
02:10:14,357 --> 02:10:18,687
These men will kill you and take it anyway.

1730
02:10:22,115 --> 02:10:24,606
No one wants to get their hands dirty.

1731
02:10:24,784 --> 02:10:27,738
Fine. I'll do it.

1732
02:10:29,414 --> 02:10:32,119
Those men on that boat? they made their choices.

1733
02:10:32,292 --> 02:10:34,581
They chose to murder and steal.

1734
02:10:34,753 --> 02:10:37,956
It doesn't make any sense for us to have to die too.

1735
02:10:47,432 --> 02:10:49,888
All the old familiar places.

1736
02:10:56,191 --> 02:10:57,270
Stand by.

1737
02:11:07,619 --> 02:11:11,202
Red team, floor secure. hostages are safe.

1738
02:11:11,414 --> 02:11:13,490
Give it to me.

1739
02:11:14,918 --> 02:11:18,666
You can tell them I took it by force.

1740
02:11:19,172 --> 02:11:24,083
Give it to me, and I'll do what you should've did 10 minutes ago.

1741
02:11:46,157 --> 02:11:49,491
We really should stop this fighting, otherwise we'll miss the fireworks.

1742
02:11:49,661 --> 02:11:51,488
There won't be any fireworks.

1743
02:11:51,913 --> 02:11:55,116
And here we go.

1744
02:12:34,456 --> 02:12:36,365
What were you trying to prove?

1745
02:12:36,541 --> 02:12:39,495
That deep down, everyone's as ugly as you?

1746
02:12:40,629 --> 02:12:41,660
You're alone.

1747
02:12:48,261 --> 02:12:50,579
Can't rely on anyone these days.

1748
02:12:50,580 --> 02:12:53,766
You gotta do everything yourself. don't we

1749
02:12:53,975 --> 02:12:56,810
That's okay. I came prepared.

1750
02:12:57,020 --> 02:12:58,672
It's a funny world we live in.

1751
02:12:58,673 --> 02:13:01,481
Speaking of which, you know how I got these scars

1752
02:13:01,650 --> 02:13:04,485
No, but I know how you got these.

1753
02:13:22,295 --> 02:13:25,047
Oh, you.

1754
02:13:25,215 --> 02:13:28,251
You just couldn't let me go, could you?

1755
02:13:29,386 --> 02:13:33,300
This is what happens when an unstoppable force...

1756
02:13:33,473 --> 02:13:37,934
...meets an immovable object.

1757
02:13:38,520 --> 02:13:43,941
You truly are incorruptible, aren't you?

1758
02:13:44,109 --> 02:13:46,813
Huh? you won't kill me...

1759
02:13:46,987 --> 02:13:53,239
...out of some misplaced sense of self-righteousness.

1760
02:13:53,410 --> 02:13:56,613
And I won't kill you...

1761
02:13:56,788 --> 02:14:00,572
...because you're just too much fun.

1762
02:14:01,626 --> 02:14:05,790
I think you and I are destined to do this forever.

1763
02:14:05,964 --> 02:14:07,956
You'll be in a padded cell forever.

1764
02:14:08,133 --> 02:14:09,960
Maybe we could share one.

1765
02:14:10,135 --> 02:14:11,593
You know, they'll be doubling up...

1766
02:14:11,761 --> 02:14:14,299
...the rate this city's inhabitants are losing their minds.

1767
02:14:14,472 --> 02:14:17,592
This city just showed you...

1768
02:14:17,767 --> 02:14:21,812
...that it's full of people ready to believe in good.

1769
02:14:21,980 --> 02:14:25,147
Until their spirit breaks completely.

1770
02:14:26,026 --> 02:14:30,853
Until they get a good look at the real Harvey Dent...

1771
02:14:31,031 --> 02:14:33,818
...and all the heroic things he's done.

1772
02:14:35,493 --> 02:14:40,535
You didn't think I'd risk losing the battle for gotham's soul...

1773
02:14:40,707 --> 02:14:43,624
...in a fistfight with you?

1774
02:14:44,169 --> 02:14:45,711
No.

1775
02:14:45,879 --> 02:14:49,295
You need an ace in the hole.

1776
02:14:49,466 --> 02:14:51,090
Mine's Harvey.

1777
02:14:51,468 --> 02:14:53,176
What did you do?

1778
02:14:53,345 --> 02:14:56,345
I took gotham's white knight...

1779
02:14:56,514 --> 02:15:00,133
...and I brought him down to our level.

1780
02:15:00,560 --> 02:15:03,514
It wasn't hard. see, madness, as you know...

1781
02:15:03,688 --> 02:15:06,725
...is like gravity.

1782
02:15:06,900 --> 02:15:09,225
All it takes is a little push.

1783
02:15:26,169 --> 02:15:27,912
Dent!

1784
02:15:48,900 --> 02:15:53,229
This is where they brought her, gordon, after your men handed her over.

1785
02:15:53,989 --> 02:15:55,566
This is where she died.

1786
02:15:55,740 --> 02:15:58,066
I know, I was here...

1787
02:15:59,119 --> 02:16:01,870
...trying to save her. - but you didn't.

1788
02:16:02,163 --> 02:16:03,907
- I couldn't. - yes, you could've.

1789
02:16:04,082 --> 02:16:05,576
If you'd listened to me.

1790
02:16:05,750 --> 02:16:08,372
If you stood up against corruption...

1791
02:16:08,545 --> 02:16:10,751
...instead of doing your deal with the devil.

1792
02:16:10,922 --> 02:16:12,547
I was trying to fight the mob!

1793
02:16:13,049 --> 02:16:17,877
You wouldn't dare try to justify yourself if you knew what I'd lost.

1794
02:16:19,180 --> 02:16:22,300
Have you ever had to talk to the person you loved most...

1795
02:16:22,475 --> 02:16:26,343
...tell them it's gonna be all right, when you know it's not?

1796
02:16:28,023 --> 02:16:31,890
Well, you're about to know what that feels like, gordon.

1797
02:16:32,652 --> 02:16:36,520
Then you can look me in the eye and tell me you're sorry.

1798
02:16:38,283 --> 02:16:41,866
- you're not going to hurt my family. - no.

1799
02:16:42,037 --> 02:16:44,741
Just the person you love most.

1800
02:16:52,756 --> 02:16:55,792
So is it your wife?

1801
02:16:56,885 --> 02:16:58,545
Put the gun down, Harvey.

1802
02:16:58,928 --> 02:17:00,588
Harvey, put down the gun.

1803
02:17:00,764 --> 02:17:04,298
Please. please, Harvey. please.

1804
02:17:05,685 --> 02:17:06,966
Oh, goddamn it.

1805
02:17:07,145 --> 02:17:09,303
Will you stop pointing that gun at my family?

1806
02:17:09,814 --> 02:17:11,474
No! - we have a winner.

1807
02:17:11,650 --> 02:17:13,144
No, jim, stop him!

1808
02:17:13,652 --> 02:17:15,478
Harvey. don't let him...

1809
02:17:15,654 --> 02:17:16,768
Harvey!

1810
02:17:18,156 --> 02:17:20,030
I'm sorry!

1811
02:17:21,826 --> 02:17:22,906
For everything.

1812
02:17:25,497 --> 02:17:27,703
Please don't hurt my son.

1813
02:17:37,842 --> 02:17:39,420
You brought your cops?

1814
02:17:39,594 --> 02:17:42,465
All they know is there's a situation.

1815
02:17:42,639 --> 02:17:45,640
They don't know who or what. they're just creating a perimeter.

1816
02:17:45,809 --> 02:17:48,478
You think I wanna escape from this?

1817
02:17:48,645 --> 02:17:51,397
There is no escape from this.

1818
02:17:51,564 --> 02:17:53,687
You don't wanna hurt the boy, Harvey.

1819
02:17:55,986 --> 02:17:59,189
It's not about what I want, it's about what's fair!

1820
02:17:59,948 --> 02:18:04,159
You thought we could be decent men in an indecent time.

1821
02:18:06,955 --> 02:18:08,034
But you were wrong.

1822
02:18:08,748 --> 02:18:12,532
The world is cruel. and the only morality in a cruel world...

1823
02:18:13,295 --> 02:18:15,204
...is chance.

1824
02:18:15,380 --> 02:18:17,088
Unbiased.

1825
02:18:17,299 --> 02:18:18,544
Unprejudiced.

1826
02:18:19,926 --> 02:18:21,041
Fair.

1827
02:18:21,219 --> 02:18:23,461
His son's got the same chance she had.

1828
02:18:24,222 --> 02:18:25,503
Fifty-fifty.

1829
02:18:25,682 --> 02:18:29,133
What happened to rachel wasn't chance. we decided to act.

1830
02:18:29,477 --> 02:18:30,806
We three.

1831
02:18:30,979 --> 02:18:34,395
Then why was it me who was the only one who lost everything?

1832
02:18:36,901 --> 02:18:39,523
- it wasn't. - the Joker chose me.

1833
02:18:39,696 --> 02:18:41,985
Because you were the best of us.

1834
02:18:42,157 --> 02:18:47,151
He wanted to prove that even someone as good as you...

1835
02:18:47,329 --> 02:18:49,072
...could fall.

1836
02:18:49,414 --> 02:18:50,694
And he was right.

1837
02:18:50,874 --> 02:18:53,116
You're the one pointing the gun, Harvey.

1838
02:18:53,293 --> 02:18:56,329
So point it at the people responsible.

1839
02:18:57,297 --> 02:18:59,124
Fair enough.

1840
02:19:02,469 --> 02:19:04,342
You first.

1841
02:19:16,858 --> 02:19:18,518
My turn.

1842
02:19:25,450 --> 02:19:27,443
Harvey, you're right.

1843
02:19:28,495 --> 02:19:31,116
Rachel's death was my fault.

1844
02:19:34,209 --> 02:19:36,664
Please don't punish the boy.

1845
02:19:37,754 --> 02:19:40,957
- please, punish me. - I'm about to.

1846
02:19:42,926 --> 02:19:44,883
Tell your boy he's gonna be all right, gordon.

1847
02:19:45,345 --> 02:19:46,969
Lie...

1848
02:19:47,472 --> 02:19:48,587
...like I lied.

1849
02:19:52,352 --> 02:19:53,930
It's going to be all right, son.

1850
02:20:32,350 --> 02:20:35,185
Dad? daddy, is he okay?

1851
02:20:51,703 --> 02:20:53,861
- thank you. - you don't have to thank me.

1852
02:20:54,497 --> 02:20:56,289
Yes, I do.

1853
02:21:00,545 --> 02:21:01,874
The Joker won.

1854
02:21:04,299 --> 02:21:07,169
Harvey's prosecution, everything he fought for...

1855
02:21:07,719 --> 02:21:09,462
...undone.

1856
02:21:09,971 --> 02:21:12,331
Whatever chance you gave us at fixing

1857
02:21:12,332 --> 02:21:14,882
Our city dies with Harvey's reputation

1858
02:21:15,060 --> 02:21:16,222
We bet it all on him.

1859
02:21:17,562 --> 02:21:20,433
The Joker took the best of us and tore him down.

1860
02:21:21,024 --> 02:21:22,435
People will lose hope.

1861
02:21:22,609 --> 02:21:24,352
They won't.

1862
02:21:26,863 --> 02:21:28,737
They must never know what he did.

1863
02:21:28,907 --> 02:21:30,734
Five dead.

1864
02:21:31,034 --> 02:21:32,314
Two of them cops.

1865
02:21:32,494 --> 02:21:34,949
- you can't sweep that... - no.

1866
02:21:39,751 --> 02:21:42,586
But the Joker cannot win.

1867
02:21:47,842 --> 02:21:51,046
Gotham needs its true hero.

1868
02:21:57,435 --> 02:22:00,472
- no. - you either die a hero...

1869
02:22:00,647 --> 02:22:05,108
...or you live long enough to see yourself become the villain.

1870
02:22:05,276 --> 02:22:07,103
I can do those things...

1871
02:22:07,529 --> 02:22:10,565
...because I'm not a hero, not like Dent.

1872
02:22:13,576 --> 02:22:16,447
I killed those people. that's what I can be.

1873
02:22:16,621 --> 02:22:18,530
No, no, you can't. you're not.

1874
02:22:18,707 --> 02:22:21,280
I'm whatever gotham needs me to be.

1875
02:22:22,961 --> 02:22:24,076
Call it in.

1876
02:22:27,382 --> 02:22:29,125
A hero.

1877
02:22:29,301 --> 02:22:32,551
Not the hero we deserved, but the hero we needed.

1878
02:22:33,138 --> 02:22:35,676
Nothing less than a knight...

1879
02:22:36,224 --> 02:22:37,932
...shining.

1880
02:22:38,560 --> 02:22:40,184
They'll hunt you.

1881
02:22:40,353 --> 02:22:42,145
You'll hunt me.

1882
02:22:42,647 --> 02:22:44,604
You'll condemn me.

1883
02:22:45,317 --> 02:22:47,605
Set the dogs on me.

1884
02:22:51,364 --> 02:22:53,653
Because that's what needs to happen.

1885
02:22:54,826 --> 02:22:56,735
Because sometimes...

1886
02:22:56,911 --> 02:22:59,070
... the truth isn't good enough.

1887
02:22:59,956 --> 02:23:02,245
Sometimes people deserve more.

1888
02:23:05,712 --> 02:23:09,626
Sometimes people deserve to have their faith rewarded.

1889
02:23:28,026 --> 02:23:29,686
Batman.

1890
02:23:31,613 --> 02:23:33,356
Batman!

1891
02:23:34,157 --> 02:23:36,114
Why's he running, dad?

1892
02:23:37,160 --> 02:23:38,488
Because we have to chase him.

1893
02:23:38,662 --> 02:23:41,532
Okay, we're going in! go, go! move!

1894
02:23:47,629 --> 02:23:49,206
He didn't do anything wrong.

1895
02:23:51,967 --> 02:23:57,553
Because he's the hero gotham deserves, but not the one it needs right now.

1896
02:23:58,974 --> 02:24:00,005
So we'll hunt him...

1897
02:24:03,144 --> 02:24:05,220
... because he can take it.

1898
02:24:07,732 --> 02:24:10,223
Because he's not our hero.

1899
02:24:17,784 --> 02:24:18,982
He's a silent guardian...

1900
02:24:20,161 --> 02:24:22,035
...a watchful protector.

1901
02:24:24,541 --> 02:24:25,821
A dark knight.

